Drop DYNAMIC_ARCH, build LAPACK in C, and keep OpenBLAS's CBLAS test directory
configurable without a Fortran compiler.

Removing enable_language(Fortran) leaves CMAKE_Fortran_COMPILER_ID empty, and
OpenBLAS 0.3.29's ctest/CMakeLists.txt:47 dereferences it unquoted:

    if (USE_OPENMP AND (${CMAKE_Fortran_COMPILER_ID} STREQUAL GNU) AND ...)

which CMake then sees as the malformed "( STREQUAL GNU )" and rejects with
"Unknown arguments specified", failing configure before anything is compiled.
That directory is added under "if(NOT NO_CBLAS)"/"if(NOT ONLY_CBLAS)", not under
BUILD_TESTING, so the BUILD_TESTING OFF below cannot avoid it, and disabling
CBLAS outright is not an option -- codon needs it. Give the variable a non-empty
value instead so the expression parses and evaluates false: all it guards is
stripping -fopenmp from Fortran flags for a GNU-Fortran + Clang-C combination
that cannot arise here anyway.

--- a/cmake/deps.cmake
+++ b/cmake/deps.cmake
@@ -156,13 +156,14 @@
     EXCLUDE_FROM_ALL YES)
 
 if(NOT APPLE)
-    enable_language(Fortran)
     CPMAddPackage(
         NAME openblas
         GITHUB_REPOSITORY "OpenMathLib/OpenBLAS"
         GIT_TAG v0.3.29
         EXCLUDE_FROM_ALL YES
-        OPTIONS "DYNAMIC_ARCH ON"
+        OPTIONS "C_LAPACK ON"
+                "$ENV{OPENBLAS_CROSS_TARGET}"
+                "CMAKE_Fortran_COMPILER_ID NONE"
                 "BUILD_TESTING OFF"
                 "BUILD_BENCHMARKS OFF"
                 "NUM_THREADS 64"
